cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ommatix in your research, cite this software."
type: software
title: "Ommatix: Spatial Indexing and Incremental Perception for GUI Agents"
authors:
  - given-names: "Juan Carlos"
    family-names: "Andrade Unigarro"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yosoyepa/Ommatix"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Ommatix is a thesis research prototype for local desktop perception. It turns
  frames into GUI elements with stable session identifiers and revisions,
  plans incremental perception against the last committed base, publishes
  immutable snapshots, and exposes observations, actions and metrics over MCP.
  Actuation is fail-closed and defaults to a dry run. Perception lives in the
  engine; reasoning lives in the agent.
keywords:
  - incremental perception
  - GUI agents
  - temporal grounding
  - spatial indexing
  - Model Context Protocol
  - Rust
  - research prototype
